# SHA-256 of every third-party asset the build downloads.
#
# scripts/setup-assets.sh and the Dockerfile both verify against this file and refuse to
# continue on a mismatch. Without it a redirected, cached or replaced download was served
# straight into the image, and because curl was called without --fail an HTTP error page was
# written to the destination as if it were the asset.
#
# The npm entries were additionally checked against the registry's own published sha512 and
# sha1 for that exact version, so the hash here is not merely a record of one download.
#
# To change a version: update the URL in setup-assets.sh and the Dockerfile, fetch the new
# file, and replace its line here with `sha256sum <file>`.
#
# <sha256>  <url>

